{"name":"Ice Cube","hex":"#afe3d6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice cube","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any small piece of ice used for cooling drinks, larger than crushed ice, and regardless of their shape.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see ice,‎ cube."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice_cube"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice Cube","blocks":[{"text":"O'Shea Jackson, known professionally as Ice Cube, is an American rapper, songwriter, actor, and film producer. His efforts on N.W.A's 1989 album Straight Outta Compton contributed to gangsta rap's popularity, and his political rap solo albums AmeriKKKa's Most Wanted (1990), Death Certificate (1991), and The Predator (1992) were all critically and commercially successful. He was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame as a member of N.W.A in 2016."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Ice_Cube_September_2025.png/330px-Ice_Cube_September_2025.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_Cube","wikidata":"Q173637"},{"title":"Ice cube","blocks":[{"text":"An ice cube is a small piece of ice, which is typically rectangular as viewed from above and trapezoidal as viewed from the side. Ice cubes are products of mechanical refrigeration and are usually produced to cool beverages. They may be made at home in a freezer with an ice tray or in an automated ice-making accessory. They may also be produced industrially and sold commercially."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ice_cubes_openphoto.jpg/330px-Ice_cubes_openphoto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_cube","wikidata":"Q488463"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"},{"title":"Cube","blocks":[{"text":"A cube is a three-dimensional solid object in geometry. It has eight vertices and twelve straight edges of the same length, so that these edges form six square faces of the same size. It is an example of a polyhedron. It is a special case of a cuboid, a parallelepiped, and a rhombohedron in which all six quadrilateral faces are squares. It is a three-dimensional hypercube, a family of polytopes that also includes the two-dimensional square and four-dimensional tesseract."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Cube-h.svg/330px-Cube-h.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cube","wikidata":"Q812880"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Ice_Cube_HS_Yearbook.jpeg/500px-Ice_Cube_HS_Yearbook.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Ice_Cube_HS_Yearbook.jpeg/500px-Ice_Cube_HS_Yearbook.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jackson as a high school senior in 1987","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIce_Cube_HS_Yearbook.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Uncle_Jam%27s_Army_-_Eazy-E_and_N.W.A._1988_Skateland_Concert_Poster.jpg/500px-Uncle_Jam%27s_Army_-_Eazy-E_and_N.W.A._1988_Skateland_Concert_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Uncle_Jam%27s_Army_-_Eazy-E_and_N.W.A._1988_Skateland_Concert_Poster.jpg/500px-Uncle_Jam%27s_Army_-_Eazy-E_and_N.W.A._1988_Skateland_Concert_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Poster for one of N.W.A's first concerts at a Compton skating rink, 1988","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUncle_Jam's_Army_-_Eazy-E_and_N.W.A._1988_Skateland_Concert_Poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Ice_Cube_and_Da_Lench_Mob_at_the_Ranch_Bowl_1993-02-10_%28ticket%29.jpg/500px-Ice_Cube_and_Da_Lench_Mob_at_the_Ranch_Bowl_1993-02-10_%28ticket%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Ice_Cube_and_Da_Lench_Mob_at_the_Ranch_Bowl_1993-02-10_%28ticket%29.jpg/500px-Ice_Cube_and_Da_Lench_Mob_at_the_Ranch_Bowl_1993-02-10_%28ticket%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A ticket from a 1993 Ice Cube concert in Omaha, Nebraska","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIce_Cube_and_Da_Lench_Mob_at_the_Ranch_Bowl_1993-02-10_(ticket).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Ice_cube_c.jpg/500px-Ice_cube_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Ice_cube_c.jpg/500px-Ice_cube_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ice Cube performing at Metro City Concert Club in October 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIce_cube_c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi